.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Plan::FieldType \- Define a field’s behavior.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 6
\&    my @sortable;
\&    for my $field ( @{ $schema\->all_fields } ) {
\&        my $type = $schema\->fetch_type($field);
\&        next unless $type\->sortable;
\&        push @sortable, $field;
\&    }
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
FieldType is an abstract class defining a set of traits and behaviors which
may be associated with one or more field names.
.PP
Properties which are common to all field types include \f(CW\*(C`boost\*(C'\fR,
\&\f(CW\*(C`indexed\*(C'\fR, \f(CW\*(C`stored\*(C'\fR, \f(CW\*(C`sortable\*(C'\fR,
\&\f(CW\*(C`binary\*(C'\fR, and \f(CW\*(C`similarity\*(C'\fR.
.PP
The \f(CW\*(C`boost\*(C'\fR property is a floating point scoring multiplier
which defaults to 1.0.  Values greater than 1.0 cause the field to
contribute more to a document’s score, lower values, less.
.PP
The \f(CW\*(C`indexed\*(C'\fR property indicates whether the field should be
indexed (so that it can be searched).
.PP
The \f(CW\*(C`stored\*(C'\fR property indicates whether to store the raw field
value, so that it can be retrieved when a document turns up in a search.
.PP
The \f(CW\*(C`sortable\*(C'\fR property indicates whether search results should
be sortable based on the contents of the field.
.PP
The \f(CW\*(C`binary\*(C'\fR property indicates whether the field contains
binary or text data.  Unlike most other properties, \f(CW\*(C`binary\*(C'\fR is
not settable.
.PP
The \f(CW\*(C`similarity\*(C'\fR property is a
Similarity object which defines matching
and scoring behavior for the field.  It is required if the field is
\&\f(CW\*(C`indexed\*(C'\fR.
